  "subject": "Descriptive statistics: describing and summarising data",
  "outOfScope": [
    "Probability, probability distributions and random variables, beyond naming the normal (bell-shaped) curve that the empirical rule describes",
    "Statistical inference: sampling distributions, confidence intervals and hypothesis tests",
    "Correlation, scatterplots and regression for two numerical variables",
    "Outlier detection methods, such as box-plot fences and z-score rules (see the Outlier detection pack)",
    "Sampling and survey design, and how the data were collected",
    "Formal measures of skewness and kurtosis, and fitting distributions to data",
    "Tooling: Excel, R, Python, Minitab and BI tools"
